course: dictionary
lesson: 5462
title: Lanyard: a word from school and sea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lanyard is a cord or strap worn round the neck to hold things like an ID card, keys or a whistle. Look at the words around it to work this out. In «Desmond comes home with a key on a lanyard», the key is hanging from something, and a lanyard is what holds it.
explain: The same word also means a short rope on a ship, used for tying or holding things. The sentence tells you which meaning is meant. A story about a school or an office is about a cord, while a story about a boat is about a rope.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If «a cord worn round the neck» fits and still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A lanyard is a cord or strap worn round the neck.
fact: Staff and visitors at school or work often wear an ID badge on a lanyard.
fact: PE teachers often have a whistle on a lanyard.
fact: «Lanyard» can also mean a short rope on a ship, used for tying or holding things.
fact: When a word has two meanings, the sentence around it tells you which one is meant.
exercise: A PE teacher blows a whistle hanging from a cord round her neck. What is that cord called? | Trousers | *Lanyard | Anchor | Sail
exercise: A sailor uses a short rope called a lanyard to tie down the sail. What is a lanyard in this story? | A school badge | A kind of cake | A cord worn round the neck | *A short rope for tying or holding things
exercise: «Desmond comes home with a key on a lanyard.» Which thing is the lanyard holding? | *A key | A thumbs-up | A bowl of pasta | A text message
test: Why might a visitor to an office wear a lanyard? | To cook dinner | To sail a boat | *To hold an ID badge | To read a book
test: A sailor on deck holds a lanyard. Which meaning fits best? | *A short rope for tying or holding things | A type of cake | A school badge | A cord round the neck
exam: Which sentence uses lanyard to mean a cord worn round the neck? | *Desmond came home with a key on a lanyard | The lanyard was a long way out to sea | Grandad made a lanyard out of bread | The sailor tied the boat with a lanyard
